== S0-E1-01 (L3 side): an invocation that declares no role
--- gov gate revoke HDG-0001 --reason x (no --role, no GOV_ROLE):
{"code": "AUTHORITY_DENIED", "message": "no acting role was declared, so the invocation carries no privileged authority (framework \u00a723: no worker behaves as an orchestrator unless explicitly assigned that role); 'revoke_gate' requires L4 (AUTHORITY_POLICY.authority_levels_required). Remediation
--- gov decide HDG-0001 --option A (no --role, no GOV_ROLE):
{"code": "AUTHORITY_DENIED", "message": "no acting role was declared, so the invocation carries no privileged authority (framework \u00a723: no worker behaves as an orchestrator unless explicitly assigned that role); 'answer_gate' requires L3 (AUTHORITY_POLICY.authority_levels_required). Remediation
--- gov gate create --question q --fields {} (no --role, no GOV_ROLE):
{"code": "AUTHORITY_DENIED", "message": "no acting role was declared, so the invocation carries no privileged authority (framework \u00a723: no worker behaves as an orchestrator unless explicitly assigned that role); 'create_gate' requires L2 (AUTHORITY_POLICY.authority_levels_required). Remediation
